                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e2387488-570d-44ae-bd9c-ce055e69ff3d",
                                "sense_id": "bd13a6d9-01ad-3b89-b058-e292abad204b",
                                "text": "Bevor er seine Möhren sät, ist er mindestens viermal übers Feld gefahren: zum Bodenauflockern und Pflügen, danach, um die 30 Zentimeter hohen Dämme zu ziehen, und schließlich zum Flämmen, um wilde Kräuter zu töten. […] Wer zu früh fährt, den bestraft das Beikraut, das die kleinen Möhrenpflänzchen erstickt.",
                                "translation": "Before he sows his carrots, he has driven across the field at least four times: to aerate the soil and to plow, then to draw the 30 cm tall dams and finally to scarf it, killing wild weeds. […] Those that drive too early are punished by weeds suffocating the litte carrot plants.",
                                "english": "Before he sows his carrots, he has driven across the field at least four times: to aerate the soil and to plow, then to draw the 30 cm tall dams and finally to scarf it, killing wild weeds. […] Those that drive too early are punished by weeds suffocating the litte carrot plants."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
